  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Security testing finds vulnerabilities before attackers do. It includes SAST, DAST, dependency scanning, and penetration testing."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Key Concepts"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "key-terms",
      "data": {
        "terms": [
          {
            "term": "SAST",
            "definition": "Static Application Security Testing: analyzing source code."
          },
          {
            "term": "DAST",
            "definition": "Dynamic Application Security Testing: testing running applications."
          },
          {
            "term": "Penetration Testing",
            "definition": "Simulating attacks to find vulnerabilities."
          },
          {
            "term": "Dependency Scanning",
            "definition": "Scanning dependencies for known vulnerabilities."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Testing Types"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "data": {
        "headers": ["Type", "When", "What It Finds"],
        "rows": [
          ["SAST", "Development", "Code vulnerabilities"],
          ["DAST", "Testing/Staging", "Runtime vulnerabilities"],
          ["SCA", "Build", "Dependency vulnerabilities"],
          ["Pentest", "Pre-release", "Exploitable vulnerabilities"]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "SAST"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Static analysis scans source code for vulnerabilities like SQL injection, XSS, and hardcoded secrets. Tools: SonarQube, Semgrep."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "DAST"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Dynamic analysis tests running applications by sending requests. Tools: OWASP ZAP, Burp Suite."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Dependency Scanning"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "SCA (Software Composition Analysis) scans dependencies for known vulnerabilities (CVEs). Tools: Snyk, Dependabot, OWASP Dependency-Check."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Penetration Testing"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Penetration testing simulates real attacks. It should be done by experts before major releases and periodically."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Architecture"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "mermaid",
